From 01dd69e223aebedfdbfeca3d5be4fb11bc78631f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 07:47:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] player information: a display on a connector that the driver
 calls DisplayPort is a matter of the connection, not of the TV input

The reason "converter" (the display is on a connector that the driver
calls DisplayPort, with no DisplayPort to HDMI converter that it takes:
an LSPCON or a dual-mode port on the board, a DisplayPort or USB-C
adapter; or the driver says so of the link, DVBRIDGE_REFUSED) was told
what the TV input asks for: its game mode and its Dolby Vision setting.
Neither changes it. It now says to connect the TV to an HDMI output that
the graphics card drives itself, without a DisplayPort or USB-C adapter
(TodoForReason(): port; Estuary's string 32729, in English and in the
three Spanish files). The two reasons of the converter of the board go
to its setting in the display settings, as before (converteron,
convertertry); those of the TV and of its link (sink, frl) stay with the
TV input. The pages of Hades for other skins are made again from
Estuary's (tools/hades-playerinfo).
